    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0397" n="293" xml:id="pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4114: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai (Cunningham)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-11T18:00:00-05:00">February 11, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Your 33, February 11, 4 p.m. I authorize you, in your discretion, to protest
                    as from your Government, against all flying of any airplanes, whether Chinese or
                    Japanese, in military service, over the International Settlement and again to
                    protest against any use whatever, by either disputant, of any part of the
                    Settlement as a base or channel in connection with military operations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
